<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">assess</ansi>

When creatures fall, their remains can be raised as undead
companions through necromantic magic. Before attempting to
reanimate a corpse, use <ansi fg="command">assess</ansi> to study it.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Usage ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">assess &lt;corpse&gt;</ansi>

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ What It Tells You ━━━</ansi>

Assessment reveals the corpse's power level and the forms of
undeath it can sustain. Weak remains can only support basic
skeletons, while stronger corpses can sustain more powerful
undead types — wraiths, golems, and other terrible forms.

Your <ansi fg="yellow">manifestation</ansi> skill determines which undead
types you can actually raise. A master necromancer can pull
forth a flesh golem from a suitable corpse where a novice
could only coax out a simple skeleton.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Important Notes ━━━</ansi>

Assessment is purely informational — you don't need to assess
a corpse before raising it. It's useful for understanding
what's available and planning your ritual.

Every undead you raise adds to your total companion count,
so factor that into your decisions.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Skill Progression ━━━</ansi>

Using <ansi fg="command">assess</ansi> trains your manifestation skill. The
more corpses you study, the better you become at gauging
their potential.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help manifestation</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help companion</ansi>
